---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | KakuCam"
  description="Privacy Policy for KakuCam. Describes how user information is handled in the app."
>
  <div class="legal-wrap">
    <p class="breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span>›</span>
      <a href="/#apps">Apps</a>
      <span>›</span>
      <a href="/apps/kakukame">KakuCam</a>
      <span>›</span>
      Privacy Policy
    </p>

    <h1>KakuCam<br />Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Established: May 28, 2026 &nbsp;/&nbsp; Last Updated: May 28, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Noveris (the "Developer") establishes this Privacy Policy regarding the handling of user information in the app "KakuCam" (the "App") as set forth below.
    </p>

    <h2>1. App Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>App Name: KakuCam</li>
      <li>Bundle ID: jp.noveris.KakuCam</li>
      <li>Developer: jp.noveris (Noveris)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The App is designed to capture and save photos, videos, GIFs, and similar content by overlaying handwritten drawings on live camera footage.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Permissions the App Uses</h2>
    <p>The App uses the following device permissions:</p>

    <h3>Camera</h3>
    <p>
      The App uses camera access to capture footage with handwritten overlays.
    </p>
    <p>
      Camera footage is processed on the device and is never transmitted to the Developer's servers.
    </p>

    <h3>Microphone</h3>
    <p>
      The App may use microphone access to record audio for videos or GIFs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Microphone access is optional. Even if microphone access is not granted, users can still record video without audio.
    </p>
    <p>
      Audio captured by the microphone is processed on the device and is never transmitted to the Developer's servers.
    </p>

    <h3>Photo Library</h3>
    <p>
      The App uses photo library access to save captured photos, videos, and GIFs to the user's device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Photo library access is used solely for the purpose of saving captured content. The App does not read existing photos or videos already in the user's photo library.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Information Stored on Device</h2>
    <p>
      To manage the Free plan usage limits, the App stores the following information on the user's device:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Daily count of video or GIF captures</li>
      <li>Date for resetting the usage limit</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This information is stored in UserDefaults on the device.
    </p>
    <p>
      This information is never transmitted to the Developer's servers or any third-party servers.
    </p>
    <p>
      If the user deletes the App, the daily count and other information stored in UserDefaults will also be deleted.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Handling of Captured Data</h2>
    <p>
      Photos, videos, GIFs, and audio captured using the App are processed on the user's device and saved to the user's photo library.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Developer does not access, view, store, analyze, or transmit any captured data externally.
    </p>
    <p>
      Temporary files such as .mov files created during recording are automatically deleted after the content is saved to the photo library.
    </p>

    <h2>5. In-App Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      The App may offer in-app purchases using Apple's StoreKit 2 to provide Pro features.
    </p>
    <p>The in-app purchase products include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>jp.noveris.kakucam.pro</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Payment processing, purchase history, and restoration for in-app purchases are handled through Apple's App Store and StoreKit 2.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Developer does not collect credit card numbers, Apple ID details, or payment method details from users.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App uses the purchase or restoration verification results provided by Apple to determine whether Pro features are accessible.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App does not transmit in-app purchase information to the Developer's own servers.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Information the App Does Not Collect or Transmit</h2>
    <p>The App does not collect or transmit the following information to the Developer's servers:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Full name</li>
      <li>Email address</li>
      <li>Phone number</li>
      <li>Physical address</li>
      <li>Location data</li>
      <li>Captured photos</li>
      <li>Captured videos</li>
      <li>Recorded audio</li>
      <li>Existing photos or videos in the photo library</li>
      <li>Advertising identifier (IDFA)</li>
      <li>Crash reports</li>
      <li>Analytics data</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The App does not incorporate Firebase, advertising SDKs, analytics SDKs, or similar third-party frameworks.
    </p>

    <h2>7. External Transmissions</h2>
    <p>
      The App does not communicate with any servers managed by the Developer.
    </p>
    <p>
      All processing related to the camera, microphone, and photo library is performed on the user's device.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, when using in-app purchases, purchase and restoration processing is handled through Apple's StoreKit 2 and App Store. In such cases, Apple's Privacy Policy and related terms apply.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>The App uses the following third-party service:</p>

    <h3>Apple StoreKit 2</h3>
    <p>
      Purpose: In-app purchase processing, purchase status verification, and restoration<br />
      Provider: Apple Inc.
    </p>
    <p>
      Payment processing through Apple StoreKit 2 is subject to Apple's Privacy Policy and related terms.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Managing Permissions</h2>
    <p>
      Users can change the camera, microphone, photo library, and other permissions granted to the App at any time through the iOS Settings app.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, if camera or photo library access is not granted, the App's core features — capturing and saving content — may not function properly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Even if microphone access is denied, users can still record video without audio.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The App does not collect or transmit personal information such as names, email addresses, location data, or captured content to the Developer's servers.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, parents or device administrators are responsible for appropriately managing device and App Store account settings.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Security</h2>
    <p>
      The App processes camera footage, microphone audio, and captured data on-device and does not transmit them to the Developer's servers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Only the minimum information necessary for managing Free plan usage limits is stored on the device.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Developer strives to design the App so that it does not collect unnecessary personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      The Developer may update this Privacy Policy as necessary.
    </p>
    <p>
      In the event of significant changes, users will be notified through the App or the Developer's website, or by other appropriate means.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy-related inquiries, please contact us at:</p>
    <ul class="legal-contact">
      <li>Developer: Noveris (Kodai Kitaura)</li>
      <li>Email: contact@noveris.jp</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="legal-nav">
      <a href="/apps/kakukame" class="secondary-button">← Back to KakuCam</a>
      <a href="/apps/kakukame/terms-en" class="secondary-button">Terms of Service →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
